# Package init files

Most directories do not need an `__init__.py`. Import the module that defines the name.

```python
from orion.datasets.events import FertiliserEvent
from orion.datasets.wheat import list_wheat_site_years
```

Do not add an `__init__.py` whose job is to list submodules or symbols with `__all__` and `_LAZY_EXPORTS`, or to eagerly re-export those names so callers can import them from the package.

Add an `__init__.py` only when the package must run code on import.
